        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Havana</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1519 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-velazquez-de-cuellar">Diego Velázquez de Cuéllar</a> founded San Cristóbal de la Habana in 1514 on the south coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>; that settlement failed, and the town that became Havana grew at its present site beside Puerto de Carenas in 1519.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the northern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> along the Straits of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, around a bay entered through a narrow inlet, with the Almendares River crossing the city from south to north.</span></div>
